In-Reply-To: <rUq8ZGDkXZ4.UXvfXWozBQAJ@knitr.groups.google.com>
References: <rUq8ZGDkXZ4.UXvfXWozBQAJ@knitr.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/knitr/c/rUq8ZGDkXZ4/m/n8aGxAo0BQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You can redefine the output hook named `chunk` to do whatever you want
to: http://yihui.name/knitr/hooks/ e.g.

local({
  hook_chunk = knitr::knit_hooks$get('chunk')
  knitr::knit_hooks$set(chunk = function(x, options) {
    out = hook_chunk(x, options)
    writeLines(out, 'your_file.tex')
  })
})

Regards,
Yihui
